# Men's Asscher Cut Ring: 3 Prong Styles That Protect

[![Men's asscher cut ring in white gold — 3 prong styles and 8-Step Octagon Rule guide](/images/mens-asscher-cut-ring-featured.jpg "Men's Asscher Ring: 3 Prong Styles That Protect — DiamondCritics")](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?Genders=men&ShapeID=Asscher&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

## TL;DR — Men's Asscher Cut Ring in One Scroll

**A men's asscher cut ring puts the only square step cut on a wide men's band. It has 8 step facets in an octagonal outline — 45° beveled corners, no sharp points. That octagonal geometry is perfect for a men's band. But the prong placement determines whether the stone stays protected for 20 years or chips in year two. The wrong prong style leaves the beveled corners exposed. The right one locks them in.**

1. **The 8-Step Octagon Rule:** Asscher's 8 step facets create a rotational "lighthouse" depth — not a linear corridor like emerald. The square shape fills a 7mm men's band differently. VS1 is still the clarity floor. Step facets expose inclusions.
2. **The 3 Prong Styles:** Corner-set 4-prong covers the beveled corners (best for active men). Side-set 4-prong opens the stone. 6-prong distributes grip across the full octagon.
3. **Natural 1ct from $2,464.** That is $676 less than a comparable emerald cut at the same quality. Asscher is the cheapest step-cut natural in this men's series.

**All solitaire settings in this guide are setting only — add your asscher cut stone. The prong style you choose determines how well the stone survives daily wear on a [men's ring](/category/mens-diamond-rings).**

