## The 8-Step Octagon Rule

Asscher cut is a square step cut with a distinctive octagonal outline. The 45° beveled corners clip the four sharp points of a square. The result is an 8-sided geometric form. That's where the name comes from.

Those 8 sides have 8 step facets arranged in concentric square rows from the table to the girdle. Unlike an emerald cut — which has long parallel rectangular planes — the asscher's step facets rotate concentrically. The reflection doesn't travel in one direction. It rotates. You get a "lighthouse" effect: a deep, spinning optical center that changes as the stone catches light.

On a [wide men's band](/category/mens-diamond-rings), that rotation is authoritative in a way emerald's linear corridor is not. Hold an asscher at any angle — the depth is there. Turn it slightly — the lighthouse rotates. The geometric center stays optically active from every viewing angle.

The rule: a 1ct asscher sits at approximately 5.5mm × 5.5mm on a 7mm men's band. That square face-up covers 78% of the band width. Add the beveled corners and the octagonal outline appears to fill the entire band face. It looks larger than the measurement suggests.

**Clarity applies the same rules as emerald.** Step facets act like a window. VS1 is the floor. VS2 inclusions are visible at close range in a step-cut stone. Never buy SI for asscher — the 8 step facets expose every inclusion in the central table.

| Clarity | Asscher Step-Facet Visibility | Men's Ring Standard | Natural 1ct Price | What this means |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FL / IF | None | Overkill at natural | $6,764+ | Don't buy; pay for lab IF instead |
| VVS1 / VVS2 | None at 10x | Premium | $2,826–$6,072 | F-VVS1 at $2,826 is the value pick |
| VS1 | None eye-clean | The floor | $2,464 | Correct; E-VS1 at $2,464 passes every test |
| VS2 | Borderline eye-clean | Risky — check GIA plot | Below $2,464 | Only if plot confirms edge inclusions |
| SI1 / SI2 | Visible to naked eye | Fail — do not buy | — | 8 step facets expose all SI inclusions |

**Verdict:** VS1 E-grade at $2,464 is the benchmark stone. It passes the 8-Step Octagon Rule eye-clean test at every viewing distance. The [1ct GIA E-VS1 at $2,464](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) paired with the [Tapered Grooved Solitaire at $1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-tapered-grooved-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147386?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = $3,464. That is the cheapest step-cut natural ring in this entire [men's diamond ring series](/category/mens-diamond-rings).

