## Asscher vs Emerald vs Cushion vs Round for Men

| Shape | 1ct Natural | Clarity Floor | Prong Risk | Band Coverage (7mm) | Character |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Asscher | [$2,464](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | VS1 mandatory | Corner placement critical | 78% × 78% | Rotational depth; octagonal authority |
| Emerald | [$3,140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | VS1 mandatory | Low — beveled corners | 100% length × 71% width | Linear depth; corridor authority |
| Cushion | [$1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | VS1 recommended | Low — no corners | 79% × 79% | Warm glow; heritage silhouette |
| Round | [$3,230](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29090690?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | VS2 acceptable | None | 93% diameter | Universal sparkle; classic |
| **What this means** | Asscher cheapest step-cut | Step cuts demand VS1 | Prong style changes durability | Asscher square fills band | Asscher: architectural, geometric, deliberate |

**Verdict:** Asscher costs less than emerald and round at natural 1ct. It delivers step-cut depth — the lighthouse rotation — at a lower entry price. The shape comparison: cushion is heritage warmth, emerald is linear authority, round is universal. Asscher is geometric precision. See the [men's emerald cut ring guide](/mens-emerald-cut-ring) and [men's cushion cut ring guide](/mens-cushion-cut-ring) for direct comparisons. For the prong question specifically — asscher is the safest step cut for active men because the beveled corners absorb more impact than emerald's right-angle corners.

