## Expert Summary

**Farzana Hasan, diamond expert** | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

Asscher is the men's ring I recommend most often when someone wants step-cut depth without the emerald price. The 8-step lighthouse rotation creates something you can't get from round, cushion, or even emerald. It's architectural. It moves as you move.

The prong choice is where most people go wrong. I've seen beautiful asschers fall out of their settings because someone picked side-set prongs for a ring that takes daily abuse. Corner-set for active men — no exceptions. The beveled corners are more durable than princess cut, but they still need coverage. Put prongs on the corners, not the sides, and the stone will stay in for 20 years.

For lab-grown, the 1.52ct D-IF at $2,795 is one of the best values in this entire series. You get the full lighthouse rotation at 6.3mm × 6.3mm. That nearly fills a 7mm men's band. The natural equivalent at 1.5ct D-IF would cost $12,000+. Rule: buy the lab version, put the savings into platinum prongs.

Pick the stone first. Apply the 8-Step Octagon Rule. Then match the prong style to your lifestyle.

Entry: [$3,464](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?Genders=men&ShapeID=Asscher&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a GIA VS1 natural on a men's grooved band. Lab 1.52ct option: [$3,795](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27991043?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

